<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- The optional integration with [XND] Nocturnal Animals (Continued), Mlie.XNDNocturnalAnimals, Workshop
       2269731409. That mod gives an animal a circadian rhythm through a def extension it owns. The source of the
       teshi gives it none, so the crepuscular rhythm below is a choice of this port, made by its owner on
       2026-09-25: a large feathered predator that is up at dawn and at dusk. With the mod absent, nothing changes.

       The patch is under PatchOperationFindMod, and that is not a precaution of comfort: the class belongs to
       Nocturnal Animals, and when it cannot be found the game does not just ignore the extension, it drops the
       whole def. Written straight into the def, this would remove the teshi for every player without the mod.

       FindMod compares the <name> of the mod, not its packageId, hence the two entries: the original title and the
       one Mlie's continuation carries. It touches only this mod's own def, so About.xml needs no loadBefore and no
       dependency, unlike the Animal Prosthetics 2 patch, which edits another mod's abstract recipes. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>[XND] Nocturnal Animals</li>
      <li>[XND] Nocturnal Animals (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Teshi"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="NocturnalAnimals.ExtendedRaceProperties">
          <bodyClock>Crepuscular</bodyClock>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
